{
  "_comment": [
    "Terms currently emitted under an official IPTC namespace that are verbatim or",
    "camelCased transliterations of a PROVIDER field name. These are the",
    "'provider-specific properties in the IPTC namespace' counter (gate 4)",
    "#027 section D4.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS A TABLE AND NOT AN INFERENCE. Nothing in the term",
    "'sport:doubleHeader' says it came from a Sportradar MLB payload. The only",
    "honest way to attribute a term to a provider is to look at the mapping that",
    "emits it and at that provider's field names, then write the attribution down",
    "where a reviewer can check it. So this table is derived by inspection of the",
    "mapping YAML listed under `derived_from`, and it is reviewable rather than",
    "magical.",
    "",
    "RELATIONSHIP TO THE UNKNOWN-TERMS COUNTER. Every term here is also an",
    "undeclared term in an official namespace, so it is also counted by the",
    "unknown-`sport:`-terms counter. That is deliberate: the two counters answer",
    "different questions ('is this a real IPTC term?' and 'whose vocabulary is this",
    "really?'). The audit reports both and states the overlap. Do not add the two",
    "together and call it a total.",
    "",
    "NOT IN THIS TABLE, ON PURPOSE: generically-named invented terms such as",
    "sport:homeScore, sport:awayScore, sport:qualifier, sport:status, sport:label,",
    "sport:year. They are invented, not provider-branded, so they belong to the",
    "unknown-terms counter alone.",
    "",
    "PR 2 removes these terms from the official namespace. It does not extend this",
    "table."
  ],
  "namespaces_in_scope": [
